@page "/opportunity"
@inject CompensationSettings Plan

<SeoHead Title="Sell QR Business Cards as an Independent Member — How Pay Works"
         Description="How QRBound members are paid: a retail commission on customer sales and small team overrides, with no fees to join, no inventory and a published income disclosure."
         Path="/opportunity" />

<section class="wrap narrow">
    <h1>Becoming a QRBound member</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Members introduce local businesses to QRBound products and are paid on what those customers buy.
        It's a sales role. Most members earn a modest amount or nothing, so read the
        <a href="/income-disclosure">income disclosure</a> first.
    </p>

    <h2>How pay works</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
        <li><strong>@Pct(Plan.RetailRate) retail commission</strong> on the volume of every customer order you refer.</li>
        <li><strong>Team overrides</strong> of @string.Join(", ", Plan.OverrideRates.Select(Pct)) on customer sales
            made by members you introduced, up to @Plan.OverrideRates.Length levels depending on rank.</li>
        <li><strong>Nothing for recruiting.</strong> Enrolling someone pays nothing; only their customers' purchases count.</li>
        <li><strong>Your own purchases can't qualify you on their own.</strong> They count toward the
            @Plan.ActiveThreshold.ToString("0") volume activity requirement only up to the volume you sell to customers.</li>
        <li><strong>A fair cap.</strong> Total payouts are capped at @Pct(Plan.PayoutCap) of sales, and no single
            team leg can supply more than @Pct(Plan.MaxLegShare) of a rank requirement.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it costs</h2>
    <p>Joining is free. There are no starter kits to buy, no monthly minimums and no inventory. If you buy
        product for yourself and change your mind, unused product can be returned within 12 months for a 90% refund.</p>

    <h2>Ranks</h2>
    <table class="table">
        <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Team customer volume</th><th>Active frontline</th><th>Override levels</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var r in Plan.Ranks)
            {
                <tr><td>@r.Rank</td><td>@r.GroupVolume.ToString("N0")</td><td>@r.ActiveFrontline</td><td>@r.PaidLevels</td></tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p><a class="btn" href="/r/qrbound?interest=Business">Talk to us about joining</a></p>
</section>

@code {
    private static string Pct(decimal d) => d.ToString("0.#%");
}
